    "xtu_rich_content_cpLaAU": {
      "type": "xtu-rich-content",
      "blocks": {
        "richtext_DXQM43": {
          "type": "richtext",
          "settings": {
            "body": "<p><strong>Format Before First Use</strong></p><p>For stable recording performance, please format the memory card in your dash cam or corresponding app before first use.</p><p><strong>1. Insert the Memory Card</strong></p><p>Insert the microSD card into the dash cam.</p><p><strong>2. Power On the Dash Cam</strong></p><p>Make sure the memory card is detected correctly.</p><p><strong>3. Format the Card</strong></p><p>Format the memory card through the dash cam settings or corresponding app.</p><p><strong>4. Start Recording</strong></p><p>Once formatting is complete, the card is ready for normal dash cam recording.</p><p><strong>Tip:</strong> Regular formatting is recommended to help maintain stable recording performance during long-term use.</p><p></p><p><strong>Learn More About Dash Cam Storage</strong></p><p>Want to learn more about memory card capacity, loop recording, formatting and storage maintenance?</p><p>Read our <a href=\"https://www.gkutech.com/blogs/guides/dash-cam-storage-guide-sd-cards-loop-recording-everything-you-need-to-know?utm_source=chatgpt.com\"><strong>Dash Cam Storage Guide</strong></a>.</p>",
            "align": "left",
            "font_size": 18,
            "font_size_mobile": 14,
            "text_color": "#333333",
            "spacing": 24,
